---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
	title="rclone Privacy Policy"
	description="Personal rclone integration privacy policy"
>
	<main class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 text-base-content">
		<article class="rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow-md md:p-10">
			<h1 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl">rclone Privacy Policy</h1>

			<div class="prose max-w-none lg:prose-lg">
				<p>
					This OAuth application is used only by the site owner for personal file
					management with rclone.
				</p>

				<h2>Data accessed</h2>
				<p>
					The application can access Google Drive files and file metadata as required
					to mount and manage the owner's Drive from their personal computer.
				</p>

				<h2>Data use and storage</h2>
				<p>
					Google Drive data is processed only for file operations initiated by the
					owner. OAuth credentials are stored locally in the owner's rclone
					configuration. This application does not operate an independent server that
					collects or stores Google Drive data.
				</p>

				<h2>Sharing</h2>
				<p>
					Google user data is not sold or shared with third parties. rclone and Google
					process data as necessary to provide their respective services.
				</p>

				<h2>Revoking access</h2>
				<p>
					Access can be revoked at any time from the Google Account connections page
					or by removing the OAuth credentials from the local rclone configuration.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>
					Questions about this application can be sent through the
					<a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
				</p>

				<p><small>Last updated: September 13, 2026</small></p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
